sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant ESP as ESP32 firmware
  participant API as Telemetry endpoint
  participant Auth as Device authentication service
  participant Service as Telemetry service
  participant DB as PostgreSQL

  ESP->>ESP: Read PZEM and validate measurement bounds
  ESP->>ESP: Build schema-v1 envelope and sample UUID
  ESP->>API: HTTPS POST + timestamp / nonce / HMAC signature
  API->>Auth: Authenticate device request
  Auth->>DB: Check active device, credential, timestamp and nonce
  Auth-->>API: Authenticated device identity
  API->>Service: Validate telemetry envelope
  Service->>DB: Insert JSONB sample (unique device + sample ID)
  DB-->>Service: Commit
  Service-->>API: Accepted
  API-->>ESP: 202 Accepted
  Note over ESP,DB: On transport failure, firmware persists the original payload in its bounded NVS queue and retries with fresh request authentication metadata.
